        {
          "id": "2d3f20fe-1d6c-371a-8173-034386cde589",
          "content": {
            "id": "2d3f20fe-1d6c-371a-8173-034386cde589",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Ben & Jerry's co-founder expects corporate conflict to continue",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: :: Ben & Jerry's co-founder says he expects to clash with the company's new owner</p><p>:: October 8, 2025</p><p>:: Vermont</p><p>:: Ben Cohen, Ben & Jerry's Co-founder</p><p>\u201cThere is no difference between how Unilever is muzzling Ben & Jerry's versus how Magnum is muzzling Ben & Jerry's. I mean, it's the same executives in Unilever that have been muzzling Ben & Jerry's as Unilever that are going to be running the Magnum Ice Cream company. And, you know, they've already demonstrated their muzzling prowess.\u201d</p><p>:: Cohen has accused Unilever of censoring Ben & Jerry's ability to speak out on progressive causes</p><p>\u201cI think what they believe is that they can have the benefits of owning Ben & Jerry's, in terms of sales and profitability, in terms of dropping money to their bottom line, without dealing with the stands that Ben & Jerry's is driven to take based on its social mission and being values led.\u201d</p><p>:: Ben & Jerry's will soon be part of Magnum Ice Cream, which is being spun off by Unilever</p><p>\u201cAnd they believe that you know, it's not a big thing. That's not a big part of the brand, it's social mission and I think they think that they can just stifle that part of it and that, you know, they'll just keep the money, you know, that they won't have to deal with the conflict. But, I mean, the conflict will still continue.\"\u00a0</p><p>The brand last year claimed in a lawsuit that Unilever had violated a hands-off policy it had agreed to under which it acknowledged the ice cream maker's independent board and its responsibility for its social mission.</p><p>Efforts to settle the lawsuit have been unsuccessful.</p><p>Unilever did not immediately respond to a request for comment.</p><p>Cohen is trying to buy back Ben & Jerry's for $1.5 billion to $2 billion with a group of investors, but said Unilever and Magnum have refused to hand over key financial information. He did not name the investors.</p><p>Cohen says he plans to keep trying to buy back the brand.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: :: Ben & Jerry's co-founder says he expects to clash with the company's new owner</p><p>:: October 8, 2025</p><p>:: Vermont</p><p>:: Ben Cohen, Ben & Jerry's Co-founder</p><p>\u201cThere is no difference between how Unilever is muzzling Ben & Jerry's versus how Magnum is muzzling Ben & Jerry's. I mean, it's the same executives in Unilever that have been muzzling Ben & Jerry's as Unilever that are going to be running the Magnum Ice Cream company. And, you know, they've already demonstrated their muzzling prowess.\u201d</p><p>:: Cohen has accused Unilever of censoring Ben & Jerry's ability to speak out on progressive causes</p><p>\u201cI think what they believe is that they can have the benefits of owning Ben & Jerry's, in terms of sales and profitability, in terms of dropping money to their bottom line, without dealing with the stands that Ben & Jerry's is driven to take based on its social mission and being values led.\u201d</p><p>:: Ben & Jerry's will soon be part of Magnum Ice Cream, which is being spun off by Unilever</p><p>\u201cAnd they believe that you know, it's not a big thing. That's not a big part of the brand, it's social mission and I think they think that they can just stifle that part of it and that, you know, they'll just keep the money, you know, that they won't have to deal with the conflict. But, I mean, the conflict will still continue.\"&nbsp;</p><p>The brand last year claimed in a lawsuit that Unilever had violated a hands-off policy it had agreed to under which it acknowledged the ice cream maker's independent board and its responsibility for its social mission.</p><p>Efforts to settle the lawsuit have been unsuccessful.</p><p>Unilever did not immediately respond to a request for comment.</p><p>Cohen is trying to buy back Ben & Jerry's for $1.5 billion to $2 billion with a group of investors, but said Unilever and Magnum have refused to hand over key financial information. He did not name the investors.</p><p>Cohen says he plans to keep trying to buy back the brand.</p></body>",
